\ Item response theory for one latent trait, after R's mirt (Chalmers, 2012) in
\ its slope-intercept parameterization: an item's chance of a correct response at
\ trait θ is g + (u − g)·σ(aθ + d), and a graded item's chance of reaching
\ category k or above is σ(aθ + d_k), its intercepts falling with k. Fitted by
\ Bock and Aitkin's EM, each item's M-step a BFGS minimize: over Gauss–Hermite
\ quadrature of a standard normal trait, or under a latent regression on
\ covariates over evenly spaced nodes. A Rasch fit (slopes 1) estimates the
\ trait's variance too. An item's standard errors are its block of the observed
\ information, so they leave out the covariance between items; a latent
\ regression's coefficient errors come from the full observed information. Each
\ item's categories are its observed values in ascending order, recoded 0..K−1
\ as mirt recodes them; a missing response is NaN.

"statistics" load-library

[ :rasch :2pl :3pl :4pl :graded ] constant irt-models

\ ---- items ----

\ the logit of a probability, held inside (1e-6, 1 − 1e-6)
: logit ( p -- x ) 1e-6 1 1e-6 - clamp dup 1 swap - / ln ; internal

\ whether an item's model has a guessing chance, :3pl or :4pl
: guessing? ( item -- flag ) :model @ dup :3pl = swap :4pl = or ; internal

\ a graded item's cumulative curves σ(aθ + d_k) at each trait value of the 1×Q row theta, one row per intercept
: graded-cumulative ( item theta -- cumulative )
	| item theta |

	theta item@slope * to slope-theta
	item@intercepts ( slope-theta + sigmoid ) map null ' vstack reduce ; internal

\ an item's category probabilities at each trait value of a 1×Q row, as K×Q, every one at least 1e-12
: item-probabilities ( item theta -- probabilities )
	| item theta |

	item@model :graded = if
		1 theta num-elements 0-matrix to zeros
		zeros 1 + item theta graded-cumulative vstack zeros vstack to cumulative
		cumulative n-rows to n-curves
		cumulative 0 n-curves 1- 0 theta num-elements submatrix
		cumulative 1 n-curves 0 theta num-elements submatrix -
	else
		item@intercepts first theta item@slope * + sigmoid item@upper item@guessing - * item@guessing + to correct
		1 correct - correct vstack
	then
	1e-12 max2 ; internal

\ the parameters the M-step searches over, unbounded: the slope unless Rasch, the intercept or a graded item's first intercept and then the logs of its gaps, and the logits of the guessing and upper chances
: item-search-vector ( item -- x )
	| item |

	item@intercepts to intercepts
	item@model :rasch = if [ ] else [ item@slope ] then
	[ intercepts first ] concat
	item@model :graded = if
		intercepts size 1- iota ( k | intercepts k @i intercepts k 1+ @i - ln ) map concat
	then
	item guessing? if [ item@guessing logit ] concat then
	item@model :4pl = if [ item@upper logit ] concat then
	vector ; internal

\ the item with the parameters of a search vector
: item-from-search ( item x -- item' )
	| item x |

	item copy to fitted
	0 to at
	item@model :rasch = not if fitted x at @e :slope ! drop ++ at then
	x at @e to intercept
	++ at
	[ intercept ] to intercepts
	item@model :graded = if
		0 item@intercepts size 1- 1 do k
			intercept x at @e exp - to intercept
			intercepts intercept add-last! drop
			++ at
		loop
	then
	fitted intercepts :intercepts ! drop
	item guessing? if fitted x at @e sigmoid :guessing ! drop ++ at then
	item@model :4pl = if fitted x at @e sigmoid :upper ! drop then
	fitted ; internal

\ the gradient over a graded item's search vector of its M-step objective, the negative log-likelihood of the expected counts, a K×Q matrix: each cumulative curve's term at a node is its slope P*(1 − P*) times the ratio of count to probability in the category below it less that in its own, the slope's derivative those terms against θ, each intercept's their sum, and a log gap's minus its exp times the intercept terms of every cumulative curve at or beyond the gap
: graded-search-gradient ( item x theta expected -- gradient )
	| item x theta expected |

	item x item-from-search to fitted
	fitted theta graded-cumulative to cumulative
	expected fitted theta item-probabilities / to ratios
	ratios dim to n-nodes to n-categories
	ratios 0 n-categories 1- 0 n-nodes submatrix
	ratios 1 n-categories 0 n-nodes submatrix -
	cumulative 1 cumulative - * * to node-terms
	node-terms row-sums to intercept-terms

	[ node-terms theta * sum intercept-terms sum ] to gradient
	1 n-categories 1- 1 do gap
		x gap 1+ @e exp negate intercept-terms gap n-categories 1- 0 1 submatrix sum * to term
		gradient term add-last! drop
	loop
	gradient vector ; internal

\ the parameters a standard error is reported for, in the reported scale: the slope unless Rasch, the intercepts, the guessing and upper chances
: item-reported-vector ( item -- x )
	| item |

	item@model :rasch = if [ ] else [ item@slope ] then
	item@intercepts concat
	item guessing? if [ item@guessing ] concat then
	item@model :4pl = if [ item@upper ] concat then
	vector ; internal

\ the item with the parameters of a reported vector
: item-from-reported ( item x -- item' )
	| item x |

	item copy to fitted
	0 to at
	item@model :rasch = not if fitted x at @e :slope ! drop ++ at then
	item@intercepts size iota ( k | x at k + @e ) map to intercepts
	at intercepts size + to at
	fitted intercepts :intercepts ! drop
	item guessing? if fitted x at @e :guessing ! drop ++ at then
	item@model :4pl = if fitted x at @e :upper ! drop then
	fitted ; internal

\ the names of an item's reported parameters, in item-reported-vector's order
: item-parameter-names ( item -- names )
	| item |

	item@model :rasch = if [ ] else [ :slope ] then
	item@intercepts size iota ( k | k "intercept-{0}" format string>symbol ) map
	item@intercepts size 1 = if drop [ :intercept ] then concat
	item guessing? if [ :guessing ] concat then
	item@model :4pl = if [ :upper ] concat then ; internal

\ ---- data ----

\ the distinct rows of responses as P×J, the number of people giving each as P×1, and each person's row among the P as N×1
: response-patterns ( responses -- patterns counts members )
	| responses |

	responses n-rows to n-people
	n-people iota ( n | responses [ n ] select-rows matrix>array ) map group-indices to groups
	n-people 1 0-matrix to members
	0 groups size 1 do p
		groups p @i 1 @i to people
		0 people size 1 do k
			members p people k @i !e drop
		loop
	loop
	responses groups ( 1 @i first ) map select-rows
	groups ( 1 @i size ) map vector
	members ; internal

\ the distinct rows of responses beside their covariates (null for none): the response patterns P×J, their covariate rows P×p or null, the number of people giving each as P×1, and each person's pattern among the P as N×1
: pattern-rows ( responses covariates -- patterns pattern-covariates counts members )
	| responses covariates |

	responses n-columns to n-items
	covariates null? if responses else responses covariates hstack then
	response-patterns to members to counts to rows
	rows 0 rows n-rows 0 n-items submatrix
	covariates null? if null else rows 0 rows n-rows n-items rows n-columns submatrix then
	counts members ; internal

\ an item's responses as an N×K indicator matrix, a row of zeros where the response is missing
: category-indicators ( column categories -- indicators )
	| column categories |

	categories ( category | column category eq ) map null ' hstack reduce ; internal

\ an item's starting parameters from its responses: slope 1, guessing 0.1 for a 3PL or 4PL and upper 0.95 for a 4PL, and intercepts the logits of the shares at or above each category above the lowest, those at the bottom of a 3PL or 4PL corrected for guessing
: starting-item ( model indicators categories -- item )
	| model indicators categories |

	indicators column-sums to counts
	counts sum to n-answered
	1 categories size 1 do k
		n-answered counts 0 1 0 k submatrix sum - n-answered /
	loop
	categories size 1- array to shares
	model :3pl = model :4pl = or if 0.1 else 0 then to guessing
	model :4pl = if 0.95 else 1 then to upper
	shares ( share | share guessing - upper guessing - / logit ) map to intercepts
	1 intercepts size 1 do k
		intercepts k @i intercepts k 1- @i 0.05 - min2 intercepts swap k !i drop
	loop
	{ :model model :slope 1 :intercepts intercepts :guessing guessing :upper upper :categories categories } ; internal

\ ---- estimation ----

\ item j's N×K indicators: its two columns of the stacked binary indicators (every item's 0 column, then every item's 1 column) when there are stacked indicators, else its own indicator matrix
: item-indicators ( indicators stacked j n-items -- item-indicators )
	| indicators stacked j n-items |

	stacked null? if indicators j @i exit then
	stacked n-rows to row-count
	stacked 0 row-count j j 1+ submatrix stacked 0 row-count n-items j + n-items j + 1+ submatrix hstack ; internal

\ every item's log-likelihood at every node summed, as N×Q: with stacked binary indicators (a matrix, see item-indicators), one product of them and the items' stacked log-probabilities; otherwise one product per item, summed as it goes
: total-log-likelihood ( items indicators theta -- log-likelihood )
	| items indicators theta |

	indicators matrix? if
		items ( item | item theta item-probabilities ln ) map to log-probabilities
		log-probabilities ( probabilities | probabilities 0 1 0 theta num-elements submatrix ) map null ' vstack reduce
		log-probabilities ( probabilities | probabilities 1 2 0 theta num-elements submatrix ) map null ' vstack reduce
		vstack to stacked-log-probabilities
		indicators stacked-log-probabilities matmul exit
	then
	null to total
	0 items size 1 do k
		indicators k @i items k @i theta item-probabilities ln matmul to term
		total null? if term else total term + then to total
	loop
	total ; internal

\ the prior weight of each node of theta, the nodes as a 1×Q row: without covariates the nodes' weights as a 1×Q row; with them, for each of the P response patterns, the normal density with the given variance about the pattern's covariates times the coefficients, normalized over the nodes, as P×Q
: trait-prior ( theta weights covariates coefficients variance -- prior )
	| theta weights covariates coefficients variance |

	covariates null? if weights transpose exit then
	theta covariates coefficients matmul - sq variance -2 * / exp to density
	density density row-sums / ; internal

\ the posterior over the nodes for every response pattern, as P×Q, and the marginal log-likelihood of the people giving them, from the summed log-likelihoods, the prior (trait-prior) and each pattern's count
: posterior ( log-likelihood prior counts -- posterior marginal )
	| log-likelihood prior counts |

	log-likelihood row-maxes to peaks
	log-likelihood peaks - exp prior * to unnormalized
	unnormalized row-sums to totals
	unnormalized totals /
	totals ln peaks + counts * sum ; internal

\ the negative marginal log-likelihood as a function of one item's reported parameters, the other items' log-likelihoods held at rest
: item-marginal-objective ( item rest indicators theta prior counts -- objective )
	| item rest indicators theta prior counts |

	( x | indicators item x item-from-reported theta item-probabilities ln matmul rest + prior counts posterior nip negate ) ; internal

\ an item's standard errors from its block of the observed information at the fit, as a frame by parameter name; null names a parameter whose block cannot be inverted
: item-standard-errors ( item rest indicators theta prior counts -- errors )
	| item rest indicators theta prior counts |

	item item-reported-vector to reported
	item rest indicators theta prior counts item-marginal-objective to objective
	( reported objective numeric-hessian inverse diagonal sqrt matrix>array ) catch if drop reported num-elements null swap array-of then to errors
	item item-parameter-names errors frame ; internal

\ a latent regression's coefficient standard errors from the full observed information: the numeric Hessian of the negative marginal log-likelihood over every item's reported parameters, the coefficients and, when estimated, the residual variance, inverted, its coefficients' diagonal entries square-rooted, as p×1; null when the information cannot be inverted
: coefficient-standard-errors ( items indicators theta pattern-covariates coefficients variance estimate-variance counts -- errors )
	| items indicators theta pattern-covariates coefficients variance estimate-variance counts |

	items ( item | item item-reported-vector ) map to item-vectors
	item-vectors ( vector | vector num-elements ) map to item-sizes
	item-sizes 0 ' + reduce to n-item-parameters
	coefficients num-elements to n-coefficients
	item-vectors null ' vstack reduce coefficients vstack
	estimate-variance if [ variance ] vector vstack then to start

	( x |
		0 to at
		[ ] to trial-items
		0 items size 1 do j
			trial-items items j @i x at at item-sizes j @i + 0 1 submatrix item-from-reported add-last! drop
			at item-sizes j @i + to at
		loop
		x at at n-coefficients + 0 1 submatrix to trial-coefficients
		estimate-variance if x at n-coefficients + @e else variance then to trial-variance
		trial-items indicators theta total-log-likelihood
		theta null pattern-covariates trial-coefficients trial-variance trait-prior
		counts posterior nip negate
	) to objective

	(
		start objective numeric-hessian inverse diagonal
		0 1 n-item-parameters n-item-parameters n-coefficients + submatrix sqrt transpose
	) catch if drop null then ; internal

\ the difficulties in IRT's usual parameterization, −d/a for each intercept
: item-difficulties ( item -- difficulties )
	| item |

	item@intercepts ( item@slope / negate ) map ; internal

\ fit an IRT model to responses, an N×J matrix, one row per person and one column per item, NaN where missing: models a symbol from irt-models for every item or an array of one per item; options a frame of :quadrature-points (61), :max-cycles (500), :tolerance (1e-4), the largest change of any search parameter between EM cycles that counts as converged, :standard-errors (1), and :covariates (none), an N×p matrix for a latent regression: each person's trait then has mean the person's covariates times the coefficients, with no intercept, integrated over :quadrature-points evenly spaced nodes on [−6, 6] as mirt does. Answers { :items :log-likelihood :cycles :converged :latent-variance :coefficients :coefficient-errors :covariates :nodes :weights }, :coefficients p×1 or null, :coefficient-errors their standard errors from the full observed information over every item parameter, the coefficients and an estimated residual variance (coefficient-standard-errors), p×1, or null without covariates, without :standard-errors or when the block cannot be inverted, :latent-variance the residual variance, :weights null under covariates; each item { :model :slope :intercepts :difficulties :guessing :upper :categories :standard-errors }
: fit-irt ( responses models options -- fit )
	| responses models options |

	responses dim to n-items to n-people
	models symbol? if models n-items array-of to models then
	models size n-items = not if n-items models size "fit-irt: {0} models for {1} items" format throw then
	models ( model | irt-models model position-of 0 < ) find-first to unknown
	unknown null? not if unknown "fit-irt: unknown model {0}" format throw then

	options :max-cycles 500 @or to max-cycles
	options :tolerance 1e-4 @or to tolerance
	models ( :rasch = ) all? to estimate-variance
	options :covariates null @or to covariates
	covariates null? if
		options :quadrature-points 61 @or gauss-hermite to weights to nodes
	else
		covariates n-rows n-people = not if n-people covariates n-rows "fit-irt: {0} covariate rows for {1} people" format throw then
		covariates nan? sum 0 > if "fit-irt: covariates have missing values" throw then
		options :quadrature-points 61 @or to n-nodes
		n-nodes iota ( k | k 12 * n-nodes 1- / 6 - ) map vector to nodes
		covariates n-columns 1 0-matrix to coefficients
	then
	responses covariates pattern-rows drop to counts to pattern-covariates to patterns

	[ ] to all-categories
	0 n-items 1 do j
		patterns j @j drop-nans matrix>array array>set set>array to categories
		categories size 2 < if j "fit-irt: item {0} has fewer than two categories" format throw then
		models j @i :graded = not categories size 2 > and if j "fit-irt: item {0} has more than two categories; model it :graded" format throw then
		all-categories categories add-last! drop
	loop

	all-categories ( categories | categories size 2 = if categories first 0 = categories last 1 = and else 0 then ) all?
	if patterns 0 eq patterns 1 eq hstack else null then to stacked
	[ ] to indicators
	stacked null? if
		0 n-items 1 do j
			indicators patterns j @j all-categories j @i category-indicators add-last! drop
		loop
	then
	stacked null? if indicators else stacked then to likelihood-indicators

	[ ] to items
	0 n-items 1 do j
		indicators stacked j n-items item-indicators to own-indicators
		items models j @i own-indicators counts * all-categories j @i starting-item add-last! drop
	loop

	1 to variance
	0 to cycles
	0 to converged
	begin cycles max-cycles < while
		covariates null? if nodes variance sqrt * else nodes then transpose to theta
		theta weights pattern-covariates coefficients variance trait-prior to prior
		items likelihood-indicators theta total-log-likelihood prior counts posterior to marginal counts * to posteriors

		stacked null? not if posteriors transpose stacked matmul transpose to all-expected then

		0 to largest-change
		0 n-items 1 do j
			items j @i to item
			stacked null? if
				indicators j @i transpose posteriors matmul
			else
				all-expected j j 1+ 0 nodes num-elements submatrix
				all-expected n-items j + n-items j + 1+ 0 nodes num-elements submatrix vstack
			then to expected
			item item-search-vector to start
			item@model :graded = if ( x | item x theta expected graded-search-gradient ) else null then to gradient
			start ( x | item x item-from-search theta item-probabilities ln expected * sum negate ) gradient 50 1e-10 minimize @estimate to found
			found start - abs max largest-change max2 to largest-change
			items item found item-from-search j !i drop
		loop

		covariates null? not if
			pattern-covariates posteriors theta transpose matmul counts / counts fit-weighted-linear to new-coefficients
			new-coefficients coefficients - abs max largest-change max2 to largest-change
			new-coefficients to coefficients
		then

		estimate-variance if
			covariates null? if theta else theta pattern-covariates coefficients matmul - then
			sq posteriors * sum n-people / to new-variance
			new-variance sqrt variance sqrt - abs largest-change max2 to largest-change
			new-variance to variance
		then

		++ cycles
		largest-change tolerance < if 1 to converged leave then
	repeat

	covariates null? if nodes variance sqrt * else nodes then to nodes
	nodes transpose to theta
	theta weights pattern-covariates coefficients variance trait-prior to prior
	items likelihood-indicators theta total-log-likelihood to log-likelihood
	log-likelihood prior counts posterior to marginal drop

	options :standard-errors 1 @or if
		0 n-items 1 do j
			items j @i to item
			indicators stacked j n-items item-indicators to own-indicators
			own-indicators item theta item-probabilities ln matmul to own
			item log-likelihood own - own-indicators theta prior counts item-standard-errors to errors
			items item errors :standard-errors ! j !i drop
		loop
		covariates null? not if
			items likelihood-indicators theta pattern-covariates coefficients variance estimate-variance counts coefficient-standard-errors to coefficient-errors
		then
	then
	items ( item | item item item-difficulties :difficulties ! ) map to items

	{ :items items :log-likelihood marginal :cycles cycles :converged converged
	  :latent-variance variance :coefficients coefficients :coefficient-errors coefficient-errors
	  :covariates covariates :nodes nodes :weights weights } ;

\ ---- bifactor ----

\ the log of each row's sum of exponentials, as r×1, from the row's largest value
: row-log-sum-exp ( m -- column )
	| m |

	m row-maxes to peaks
	m peaks - exp row-sums ln peaks + ; internal

\ the given columns of a matrix
: select-columns-of ( m columns -- m' ) swap transpose swap select-rows transpose ; internal

\ an item's log-probabilities of a correct and an incorrect response at each node of a 1×C row of general trait values and a 1×C row of specific trait values (0 for an item on the general trait only): [ correct incorrect ], each 1×C
: bifactor-log-probabilities ( item general specific -- logs )
	| item general specific |

	general item@slope * specific item@specific-slope * + item@intercepts first + sigmoid to p
	[ p 1e-12 max2 ln 1 p - 1e-12 max2 ln ] ; internal

\ the log-likelihood of each response pattern's answers to the member items at each node of 1×C rows of general and specific trait values, as P×C, from the patterns' correct and incorrect indicators for those items (P×members)
: bifactor-items-log-likelihood ( items members correct incorrect general specific -- log-likelihood )
	| items members correct incorrect general specific |

	members ( j | items j @i general specific bifactor-log-probabilities ) map to logs
	correct logs ( first ) map null ' vstack reduce matmul
	incorrect logs ( 1 @i ) map null ' vstack reduce matmul + ; internal

\ the bifactor E-step at the items, the specific factors in parallel (pmap): the marginal log-likelihood summed over the people giving each response pattern, each pattern's posterior over the general nodes (P×Q), and per specific factor [ conditional integrated ]: conditional the posterior over the specific nodes at each pattern and general node ((P·Q)×Q), integrated the log of the specific factor's likelihood summed over its nodes ((P·Q)×1); each factor's exponentials are computed once and serve both. layout is fit-bifactor's frame of fixed quantities
: bifactor-e-step ( items layout -- marginal general-posterior factor-terms )
	| items layout |

	layout@n-patterns to n-patterns
	layout@n-nodes to n-nodes
	layout@general-items size 0 > if
		items layout@general-items layout@general-correct layout@general-incorrect layout@general-row 0 bifactor-items-log-likelihood
	else
		n-patterns n-nodes 0-matrix
	then to by-general
	layout@factor-items size iota
	( f |
		items layout@factor-items f @i layout@factor-correct f @i layout@factor-incorrect f @i
		layout@grid-general layout@grid-specific bifactor-items-log-likelihood
		n-patterns n-nodes * n-nodes reshape layout@log-weight-row + to inner
		inner row-maxes to peaks
		inner peaks - exp to shifted
		shifted row-sums to sums
		[ shifted sums / sums ln peaks + ]
	) pmap to factor-terms
	factor-terms ( term | term 1 @i n-patterns n-nodes reshape ) map by-general ' + reduce
	layout@log-weight-row + to weighted
	weighted row-log-sum-exp to pattern-log-likelihood
	pattern-log-likelihood layout@counts * sum
	weighted pattern-log-likelihood - exp
	factor-terms ; internal

\ an item's slopes and intercept after Newton steps on its expected counts, each step held within ±1 per parameter so a nearly singular information matrix cannot throw the item off: correct (1×C) and answered (1×C) at the nodes, the design C×K of the nodes' general value, specific value when the item has a specific factor, and 1; answers the item and the largest change of a parameter
: bifactor-m-step ( item correct answered design -- item' change )
	| item correct answered design |

	item@group 0 = if
		[ item@slope item@intercepts first ]
	else
		[ item@slope item@specific-slope item@intercepts first ]
	then vector to start
	start to beta
	0 5 1 do step
		design beta matmul sigmoid to p
		correct transpose answered transpose p * - to residual
		design transpose residual matmul to gradient
		answered transpose p * 1 p - * to w
		design transpose design w * matmul to information
		information gradient fit-linear -1 max2 1 min2 to delta
		beta delta + to beta
		delta abs max 1e-10 < if leave then
	loop
	item copy to fitted
	fitted beta 0 @e :slope ! drop
	item@group 0 = if
		fitted [ beta 1 @e ] :intercepts ! drop
	else
		fitted beta 1 @e :specific-slope ! drop
		fitted [ beta 2 @e ] :intercepts ! drop
	then
	fitted beta start - abs max ; internal

\ the fixed quantities of a bifactor E-step for responses (N×J, 0, 1 or NaN) and item groups at
\ n-nodes Gauss–Hermite nodes per dimension: the nodes and weights, the general and grid rows and
\ designs, the response patterns' indicators split by item set (and transposed for the M-step),
\ the patterns' counts and each person's pattern (:members)
: bifactor-layout ( responses groups n-nodes -- layout )
	| responses groups n-nodes |

	responses n-columns to n-items
	n-nodes gauss-hermite to weights to nodes
	nodes transpose to general-row
	weights transpose ln to log-weight-row
	n-nodes n-nodes * to n-grid
	n-grid iota ( c | nodes c n-nodes % nip @e ) map vector transpose to grid-general
	n-grid iota ( c | nodes c n-nodes % drop @e ) map vector transpose to grid-specific
	grid-general transpose grid-specific transpose hstack n-grid 1 0-matrix 1 + hstack to grid-design
	general-row transpose n-nodes 1 0-matrix 1 + hstack to general-design
	groups array>set set>array ( group | group 0 > ) filter to factors
	n-items iota ( j | groups j @i 0 = ) filter to general-items
	factors ( factor | n-items iota ( j | groups j @i factor = ) filter ) map to factor-items
	responses null pattern-rows to members to counts drop to patterns
	patterns n-rows to n-patterns
	patterns 1 eq to correct-indicators
	patterns 0 eq to incorrect-indicators
	correct-indicators incorrect-indicators + to answered-indicators
	correct-indicators general-items select-columns-of to general-correct
	incorrect-indicators general-items select-columns-of to general-incorrect
	factor-items ( members | correct-indicators members select-columns-of ) map to factor-correct
	{ :nodes nodes :weights weights :general-items general-items :factor-items factor-items :factors factors
	  :general-correct general-correct :general-incorrect general-incorrect
	  :factor-correct factor-correct
	  :factor-incorrect factor-items ( members | incorrect-indicators members select-columns-of ) map
	  :general-correct-rows general-correct transpose
	  :general-answered-rows answered-indicators general-items select-columns-of transpose
	  :factor-correct-rows factor-correct ( correct | correct transpose ) map
	  :factor-answered-rows factor-items ( members | answered-indicators members select-columns-of transpose ) map
	  :general-row general-row :grid-general grid-general :grid-specific grid-specific :log-weight-row log-weight-row
	  :general-design general-design :grid-design grid-design
	  :n-patterns n-patterns :n-nodes n-nodes :counts counts :members members } ; internal

\ fit a bifactor 2PL to binary responses, an N×J matrix of 0, 1 and NaN for missing: groups, an array of J whole numbers, gives each item's specific factor, or 0 for an item on the general trait only, and every specific factor needs at least two items; each item's chance of a correct response is σ(a·θg + c·θs + d), the general trait θg and the specific traits independent standard normals. Bock and Aitkin's EM over the distinct response patterns with Gibbons and Hedeker's dimension reduction: each specific factor is integrated at every general node, over :quadrature-points (21) Gauss–Hermite nodes per dimension, so the work is two-dimensional whatever the number of specific factors; each item's M-step is Newton steps on its expected counts. Options also :max-cycles (500) and :tolerance (1e-4), the largest change of any parameter between cycles that counts as converged. Answers { :items :log-likelihood :cycles :converged :nodes :weights :bifactor }, :log-likelihood at the returned items, :bifactor 1; each item { :model :slope :specific-slope :group :intercepts :difficulties }, :specific-slope 0 for an item on the general trait only
: fit-bifactor ( responses groups options -- fit )
	| responses groups options |

	responses n-columns to n-items
	groups size n-items = not if n-items groups size "fit-bifactor: {0} groups for {1} items" format throw then
	groups ( group | group 0 < group group ftruncate = not or ) find-first to bad-group
	bad-group null? not if bad-group "fit-bifactor: group {0} is not a whole number from 0 up" format throw then
	responses 0 eq responses 1 eq + responses nan? + 0 eq sum 0 > if "fit-bifactor: responses must be 0, 1 or NaN" throw then
	options :max-cycles 500 @or to max-cycles
	options :tolerance 1e-4 @or to tolerance
	options :quadrature-points 21 @or to n-nodes
	groups array>set set>array ( group | group 0 > ) filter to factors
	factors ( factor | n-items iota ( j | groups j @i factor = ) filter ) map to factor-items
	factors size iota ( f | factor-items f @i size 2 < ) find-first to lone-factor
	lone-factor null? not if factors lone-factor @i "fit-bifactor: specific factor {0} has fewer than two items" format throw then
	responses groups n-nodes bifactor-layout to layout
	layout@nodes to nodes
	layout@weights to weights
	layout@general-design to general-design
	layout@grid-design to grid-design
	layout@general-items to general-items
	layout@general-correct-rows to general-correct-rows
	layout@general-answered-rows to general-answered-rows
	layout@factor-correct-rows to factor-correct-rows
	layout@factor-answered-rows to factor-answered-rows
	layout@n-patterns to n-patterns
	layout@counts to counts
	n-nodes n-nodes * to n-grid

	[ ] to items
	0 n-items 1 do j
		responses j @j drop-nans to answered
		answered num-elements 0 = if j "fit-bifactor: item {0} has no responses" format throw then
		answered mean 1e-3 1 1e-3 - clamp to share
		groups j @i 0 = if 0 else 0.5 then to specific-slope
		items { :model :2pl :slope 1 :specific-slope specific-slope :group groups j @i
		  :intercepts [ share logit ] :guessing 0 :upper 1 :categories [ 0 1 ] } add-last! drop
	loop

	options :progress 0 @or to progress
	0 to cycles
	0 to converged
	begin cycles max-cycles < while
		items layout bifactor-e-step to factor-terms counts * to general-posterior to cycle-log-likelihood

		[ ] to updates
		general-items size 0 > if
			general-correct-rows general-posterior matmul to all-correct
			general-answered-rows general-posterior matmul to all-answered
			general-items size iota ( position |
				general-items position @i to j
				items j @i all-correct position @i all-answered position @i general-design bifactor-m-step
				to change to fitted [ j fitted change ]
			) pmap to updates
		then
		factors size iota ( f |
			factor-items f @i to members
			factor-terms f @i first general-posterior n-patterns n-nodes * 1 reshape * n-patterns n-grid reshape to posterior
			factor-correct-rows f @i posterior matmul to all-correct
			factor-answered-rows f @i posterior matmul to all-answered
			members size iota ( position |
				members position @i to j
				items j @i all-correct position @i all-answered position @i grid-design bifactor-m-step
				to change to fitted [ j fitted change ]
			) map
		) pmap [ ] ' concat reduce updates swap concat to updates
		0 to largest-change
		0 updates size 1 do index
			updates index @i to update
			items update 1 @i update first !i drop
			update 2 @i largest-change max2 to largest-change
		loop
		progress if largest-change cycle-log-likelihood cycles 1+ "cycle {0:d}: log-likelihood {1:.1f}, largest change {2:.2e}" format print cr then

		++ cycles
		largest-change tolerance < if 1 to converged leave then
	repeat

	items layout bifactor-e-step drop drop to marginal
	items ( item | item item item-difficulties :difficulties ! ) map to items
	{ :items items :log-likelihood marginal :cycles cycles :converged converged :nodes nodes :weights weights :bifactor 1 } ;

\ every person's bifactor trait vector, general then specific 1..S, and its standard errors, from a
\ fit-bifactor fit and binary responses in the fit's columns: method :eap, the posterior means and
\ standard deviations over the fit's nodes by the same dimension reduction as the fit, or :map, the
\ posterior mode under the standard normal traits by minimize from the EAP, its errors from the
\ curvature there. Answers { :theta :se }, each N×(1+S)
: bifactor-scores ( fit responses method -- scores )
	| fit responses method |

	fit :bifactor 0 @or not if "bifactor-scores: the fit is not a bifactor fit" throw then
	fit@items to items
	items ( item | item@group ) map to groups
	responses groups fit@nodes num-elements bifactor-layout to layout
	layout@n-patterns to n-patterns
	layout@n-nodes to n-nodes
	layout@nodes to nodes
	items layout bifactor-e-step to factor-terms to general-posterior drop
	general-posterior nodes matmul to general-means
	general-posterior nodes sq matmul general-means sq - 0 max2 sqrt to general-errors
	layout@factors size iota ( f |
		factor-terms f @i first general-posterior n-patterns n-nodes * 1 reshape * n-patterns n-nodes n-nodes * reshape to joint
		joint layout@grid-specific transpose matmul to means
		[ means joint layout@grid-specific sq transpose matmul means sq - 0 max2 sqrt ]
	) map to specific
	specific ( pair | pair first ) map general-means ' hstack reduce to means
	specific ( pair | pair 1 @i ) map general-errors ' hstack reduce to errors
	method :eap = if { :theta means layout@members select-rows :se errors layout@members select-rows } exit then
	method :map = not if method "bifactor-scores: unknown method {0}; :eap or :map" format throw then

	layout@factors size 1+ to n-traits
	n-patterns n-traits 0-matrix to modes
	n-patterns n-traits 0-matrix to mode-errors
	responses null pattern-rows drop drop drop to patterns
	0 n-patterns 1 do n
		patterns [ n ] select-rows to row
		( x |
			0
			0 items size 1 do j
				row 0 j @i,j to response
				response nan? not if
					items j @i to item
					x 0 @e item@slope * item@group 0 = if 0 else x item@group @e item@specific-slope * then +
					item@intercepts first + sigmoid 1e-12 1 1e-12 - clamp to p
					response 1 = if p else 1 p - then ln +
				then
			loop
			x sq sum 2 / - negate
		) to objective
		means [ n ] select-rows transpose to start
		start objective null 100 1e-10 minimize @estimate to mode
		0 n-traits 1 do k modes mode k @e n k !i,j drop loop
		mode objective numeric-hessian inverse diagonal sqrt to curvature-errors
		0 n-traits 1 do k mode-errors curvature-errors 0 k @i,j n k !i,j drop loop
	loop
	{ :theta modes layout@members select-rows :se mode-errors layout@members select-rows } ;

\ ---- scoring ----

\ every person's trait estimate and its standard error from a fit and the responses it was fitted to, or new ones in the same columns: method :eap, the posterior mean and standard deviation over the fit's nodes, or :map, the posterior mode under the fitted normal trait by minimize from the EAP, its error from the curvature there. A fit with covariates scores the people it was fitted to, each under the trait's mean from their covariates. Answers { :theta :se }, n×1 vectors
: irt-scores ( fit responses method -- scores )
	| fit responses method |

	fit :bifactor 0 @or if "irt-scores: a bifactor fit has no single trait to score" throw then
	fit@items to items
	fit@nodes transpose to theta
	fit@covariates to covariates
	covariates null? not if
		covariates n-rows responses n-rows = not if covariates n-rows responses n-rows "irt-scores: {0} response rows for a fit to {1} people" format throw then
	then
	responses covariates pattern-rows to members to counts to pattern-covariates to patterns
	theta fit@weights pattern-covariates fit@coefficients fit@latent-variance trait-prior to prior
	items size iota ( j | patterns j @j items j @i @categories category-indicators ) map to indicators
	items indicators theta total-log-likelihood prior counts posterior drop to posteriors
	posteriors theta transpose matmul to means
	posteriors theta sq transpose matmul means sq - 0 max2 sqrt to errors
	method :eap = if { :theta means members select-rows :se errors members select-rows } exit then
	method :map = not if method "irt-scores: unknown method {0}; :eap or :map" format throw then

	fit@latent-variance to variance
	patterns n-rows to n-patterns
	n-patterns 1 0-matrix to modes
	n-patterns 1 0-matrix to mode-errors
	covariates null? if n-patterns 1 0-matrix else pattern-covariates fit@coefficients matmul then to prior-means
	0 n-patterns 1 do n
		indicators ( person-indicators | person-indicators n @i ) map to person
		prior-means n @e to prior-mean
		( x |
			items size iota ( j | person j @i items j @i x item-probabilities ln matmul first ) map 0 ' + reduce
			x first prior-mean - sq variance 2 * / - negate
		) to objective
		[ means n @e ] vector objective null 100 1e-10 minimize @estimate to mode
		modes mode first n !e drop
		mode-errors mode objective numeric-hessian first 1 swap / sqrt n !e drop
	loop
	{ :theta modes members select-rows :se mode-errors members select-rows } ;

\ an item's Fisher information at trait values. For a fit-irt fit, thetas an array or vector of
\ trait values, answered as n×1: a dichotomous item's P′²/(P(1 − P)), P′ = (u − g)·a·σ(1 − σ), and a
\ graded item's Σ_k P_k′²/P_k over its categories. For a fit-bifactor fit, thetas n×(1+S), each row a
\ general value then the specific ones, answered as n×3: the item's information on the general trait,
\ on its specific trait and between them, p(1 − p) times a², c² and a·c (the specific columns 0 for an
\ item on the general trait only)
: item-information ( fit item thetas -- information )
	| fit item thetas |

	fit@items item @i to fitted
	fit :bifactor 0 @or if
		thetas 0 thetas n-rows 0 1 submatrix to general
		fitted@group 0 = if thetas n-rows 1 0-matrix else thetas fitted@group @j then to specific
		general fitted@slope * specific fitted@specific-slope * + fitted@intercepts first + sigmoid to p
		p 1 p - * to spread
		spread fitted@slope sq * spread fitted@specific-slope sq * hstack spread fitted@slope fitted@specific-slope * * hstack
		exit
	then
	thetas matrix? if thetas as-column else thetas vector then transpose to theta
	fitted@model :rasch = if 1 else fitted@slope then to slope
	fitted@model :graded = if
		fitted theta graded-cumulative to cumulative
		cumulative 1 cumulative - * slope * to rising
		1 theta num-elements 0-matrix to zeros
		zeros rising vstack zeros vstack to padded
		padded n-rows to n-rows-padded
		padded 0 n-rows-padded 1- 0 theta num-elements submatrix
		padded 1 n-rows-padded 0 theta num-elements submatrix - to derivatives
		derivatives sq fitted theta item-probabilities / column-sums transpose exit
	then
	fitted@intercepts first theta slope * + sigmoid to s
	s 1 s - * slope * fitted@upper fitted@guessing - * to derivative
	fitted theta item-probabilities 1 2 0 theta num-elements submatrix to p
	derivative sq p 1 p - * / transpose ;

\ an item's category probabilities at trait values, an array or vector, as a matrix of one row per value and one column per category
: irt-probabilities ( fit item thetas -- probabilities )
	| fit item thetas |

	fit :bifactor 0 @or if "irt-probabilities: a bifactor item's curves depend on two traits" throw then
	fit@items item @i thetas matrix? if thetas as-column else thetas vector then transpose item-probabilities transpose ;
